#: Game.Levels.Demo
msgid "Four levels, grammars from three eras of generative syntax — for English, Turkish and\n"
"Swahili — written in one formal language. Each grammar is data: categories, a lexicon, rules. The same derivation relation,\n"
"checked by Lean, decides what each grammar generates."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Demo.L04_MP
msgid "Narrow syntax for *mtoto atalala*."
msgstr ""

#: Game
msgid "This demo shows one formal language expressing grammars from three eras of generative syntax:\n"
"\n"
"1. a linear grammar (English),\n"
"2. X-bar theory with GB modules — c-selection, Case, EPP, θ, Move α — for Turkish, head-final,\n"
"3. the Minimalist Program of the workspace era (MERGE on workspaces, labeling, interface\n"
"   conditions) for Swahili.\n"
"\n"
"The language is Bare Grammar (Keenan & Stabler 2003), implemented in Lean 4. A grammar is\n"
"data — categories, a lexicon, rules — and an expression belongs to the language when there is\n"
"a derivation of it. Every step you take is checked by Lean's kernel."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Demo.L04_MP
